<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12211" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπλοος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπλους</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ουν</span>: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			
				Act.
			, of ships, <i>unseaworthy,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριήρεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					3.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦς ἄπλους ποιεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.34
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆες ἅπλοι ἐγένοντο</span>
			ibid.: of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναύκληρον . . ποιήσας ἄπλουν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Crito Com.
					3
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπλοώτεραι νῆες</span>”
				<i>less fit for sea,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.60
				</span></i>
			 (codd.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπλούστεραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Suid.
				</span></i>
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, of the sea, <i>not navigable, closed to navigation</i>
			(cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπλοια</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἄπλους ἡ θάλαττα ὑπὸ τῶν . .
					λῃστῶν γέγονεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.241
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλμη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1271
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πόντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					4.38.7
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰθήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					6.358
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>no seafarer,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἠχώ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				319
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
